1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means a copyright holder identified in the Software's applicable
notices, to the extent that holder has authority to grant the relevant rights.

"Project Licensor" means 阿勒泰自由意文化服务有限责任公司, publishing as
FAD Records. legal/PROJECT-LICENSOR.md records this fixed company identity for
reference. Contributors, maintainers, licensees and repository administrators
do not become the Project Licensor merely by holding those roles. Changing a
fork, owner, notice or identity file cannot redirect this grant to another
beneficiary. A lawful successor must establish the relevant transferred rights;
a later document edit does not retroactively substitute a beneficiary.

"Engine Modification" means a change to, derivative of, or addition incorporated
into the Engine's implementation or interfaces, including related Engine tests
and build changes necessary for that modification. Merely linking or calling
an unchanged Engine does not make an independent application, plugin wrapper,
UI, brand, music, preset or asset an Engine Modification.

"Community Improvement" means an Engine Modification you own or are authorized
to license and that you deliberately distribute or make publicly available in
exercise of the Community rights under this version. It does not include a
private, undistributed modification or an unrelated independent module.

"Software" means the FAD Engine code, examples, documentation and development
skills in this repository, including modifications, except material expressly
covered by a separate third-party license. It does not include FAD Synth, FAD
product UI, ALT, models or training data, factory presets, commercial audio or
visual assets, account systems, commerce code, or production services.

"Covered Product" means a plugin, application, library, service, hardware
product, or other software offering that contains, links to, embeds, or uses the
Software as a material part of its delivered functionality.

"Complete Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying the
specific Covered Product version, including the Software and its modifications,
integration code, parameter and state definitions, and the build scripts and
configuration needed to build that version. Separately available, unmodified
general-purpose compilers, operating systems and system libraries need not be
copied. Other dependencies may be supplied through lawful, working retrieval
instructions that identify the required versions and applicable licenses.
Private credentials, signing keys and user data must not be included.

"Community Distribution" means distribution of a Covered Product that is
available to every recipient without a mandatory payment or paid entitlement,
with public, no-charge access to its Complete Corresponding Source. A trial,
time-limited evaluation of a paid product, paid bundle, purchase-dependent
download, premium feature tier, or payment-gated update is not Community
Distribution. Merely publishing the Engine part of a closed product is not
Complete Corresponding Source.

"Commercial Use" means selling or licensing a Covered Product for consideration,
charging for access to its Engine-powered functionality, incorporating it into
a paid bundle or commercial hardware offering, operating an Engine-powered paid
service, or a use separately designated as commercial by written agreement with
the Licensor. Commercial Use does not include the permitted musical output or
the unconditional donations described below.

