3. DISTRIBUTION CONDITIONS

For every Community Distribution, you must:

(a) Include this license and preserve applicable copyright, attribution,
third-party license and notice information. Identify material modifications
without suggesting the original authors endorse them.

(b) Provide a prominent, working link or accompanying source package giving
public, no-charge access to the Complete Corresponding Source for that exact
released version. Source access must not require a purchase, donation, paid
account, non-disclosure agreement or individualized permission. Normal public
code-host access and download mechanisms are acceptable.

(c) Make source available no later than the corresponding binary or service
release, throughout the time you offer it, and for at least three years after
your last distribution of that version. If the host becomes unavailable,
restore access through another public location without unreasonable delay.

(d) Permit recipients to inspect, modify and redistribute your contributions
and integration code as necessary to exercise the same Community rights. You
may apply a compatible, more permissive license to your own contributions, but
may not grant commercial or closed-source rights to the underlying Software
that you do not hold. Additional terms must not defeat this license or prevent
rebuilding and modifying the corresponding version. The Project Licensor's
separate rights under section 7A or an accepted contributor agreement are not
limited by this paragraph.

(e) Keep the Covered Product available without payment-gated functionality,
downloads, updates, early access or exclusive editions. Do not impose technical
or contractual restrictions that negate the rights granted here.

(f) For each Community Improvement, make the express grant in section 7A and
publish a grant notice with the corresponding source. Identify the rights
holder, affected paths/commit or release, this license version and the Project
Licensor. Use legal/IMPROVEMENT-GRANT-NOTICE.md or an equivalent clear statement.
A required authority record may be supplied privately to the Project Licensor;
do not publish personal addresses, identity documents or private signatures.
A licensee unable to grant these rights must obtain a separate agreement before
distributing the affected modification under these Community terms.

These conditions apply to binaries and source distributions alike. Distributing
a modified Engine on its own is also subject to this license.

